# Linear channel adapter — webhook receive + GraphQL send
#
# ── LINEAR_API_KEY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A personal API key. The agent posts comments AS the user who owns this
# key, so create one for a service account if you don't want comments to
# look like they came from a human teammate.
#
# Mint at: https://linear.app/settings/api → "Personal API keys" → "Create
# key". Scope is implicit (full account access); there is no granular
# selection in Linear's UI today.
#
# Treat as a secret. Anyone with this key can read/write the team's data.
LINEAR_API_KEY=

# ── LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used to HMAC-SHA256 sign every webhook POST. Linear puts the hex digest in
# the `Linear-Signature` header; receive() verifies it constant-time and
# throws on mismatch so the agent's HTTP layer returns 401 (no silent drop).
#
# Configure at: https://linear.app/settings/api/webhooks → "New webhook"
#   • URL: https://<your-deploy>/channels/linear
#   • Resources: tick "Comments" and "Issues"
#   • Signing secret: Linear generates one per webhook — paste it below.
#
# Docs: https://linear.app/developers/webhooks#securing-webhooks
LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Operational notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# • The adapter only forwards Issue/create and Comment/create today (Linear
#   also delivers update + remove for both — we drop them as null). If you
#   want the agent to react to issue edits or status changes, extend the
#   switch in receive() and pass the action through.
#
# • send() always creates a Comment on the issue id you got from receive().
#   To create a brand-new issue from the agent, use issueCreate(input:
#   IssueCreateInput!) — different mutation, not wired here.
#
# • GraphQL endpoint: https://api.linear.app/graphql
#   GraphQL schema docs: https://linear.app/developers/graphql
#
# • Webhook payload reference (fields receive() reads):
#   https://linear.app/developers/webhooks#payload-format
